course: dictionary
lesson: 8870
title: Shortcut
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A shortcut is a quicker or shorter way to get somewhere, or to get something done. The words around it give you clues. «A canal is a waterway dug by people, a shortcut where nature left none.» A canal is dug by people, so here a shortcut is a quicker route that people make where no path exists.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. "A canal is a quicker route dug by people" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Ollie tried a shortcut: he secretly downloaded the free demo of an older game on the family console.» The words after the colon explain the shortcut: Ollie got a game in a quick way. The word "secretly" is a clue that the author is not simply praising it.
fact: A shortcut is a quicker or shorter way to get somewhere.
fact: In maths, a shortcut is a quick trick, such as moving the digits to multiply a number by 10.
fact: On a computer, a shortcut is a key combination or icon that does something quickly, like Ctrl+C to copy.
fact: «Don't take shortcuts through the woods or across railway lines.» This is a safety warning: a shorter route can still be dangerous.
fact: «There are no shortcuts to learning» means you have to practise to get better.
exercise: «A canal is a waterway dug by people, a shortcut where nature left none.» What does shortcut mean in this sentence? | A long way round the hill | A park with lots of trees | *A quicker route where there was no path before | A waterway that nature made by itself
exercise: Why does the warning say «Don't take shortcuts through the woods or across railway lines»? | The woods and railway lines are always closed | Shortcuts are always slower than the normal way | Railway lines are too wide to cross | *A shorter route through these places can be dangerous
exercise: «Ollie tried a shortcut: he secretly downloaded the free demo.» Find and copy one word that shows Ollie did it in secret. | tried | downloaded | *secretly | family
test: On a computer, what does the shortcut Ctrl+C do? | Pastes the text | Saves the file as a new name | *Copies the text | Closes the window
test: In mental maths, what is a shortcut for multiplying a number by 10? | *Move each digit one place to the left and add a zero | Multiply the number by 100 and then halve it | Count up in ones | Add ten to the number
exam: «There are no shortcuts to learning.» What does this phrase mean? | Learning only happens in a school building | You can skip the practice and still get better | *You have to practise and work hard to get better | Learning is always quick and easy
